---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About - Thinking Buffer">
	<!-- Hero Section -->
	<section class="about-hero">
		<div class="hero-content">
			<h1>About Thinking Buffer</h1>
			<p class="subtitle">A space to pause, process, and translate technical lessons and timeless wisdom into modern guides and visual stories.</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<div class="about-split">
		<!-- Left Column: The Philosophy -->
		<section class="philosophy-section">
			<h2 class="section-title">The Philosophy of the Buffer</h2>
			
			<div class="narrative">
				<h3>Why "Thinking Buffer"?</h3>
				<p>
					In computer science, a buffer is a temporary holding space—a place where data pauses before being processed and sent to its final destination. In our fast-paced lives and careers, we often lack that space. We react to messages, deadlines, and challenges instantly, operating on muscle memory and automatic patterns.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>Thinking Buffer</strong> is a dedicated digital canvas designed to serve as that pause. It is a space to slow down, capture thoughts, examine situations from alternative angles, and process them before releasing them into the world.
				</p>

				<h3>Abstracting the Office</h3>
				<p>
					Every day at work, we face challenges, solve complex systems problems, and navigate human interactions. But these experiences shouldn't stay locked behind corporate walls. 
				</p>
				<p>
					My goal is to capture what I learn in my professional life and abstract those experiences into general, actionable frameworks. By distilling specific technical and leadership situations into broader principles, these lessons become tools that other builders, engineers, and leaders can leverage.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- Right Column: Neerav Profile -->
		<section class="profile-section">
			<div class="card profile-card">
				<div class="profile-avatar-large">
					<img src="/images/neerav_avatar.jpg" alt="Neerav Kumar" />
				</div>
				<h2 class="profile-name">Neerav Kumar</h2>
				<p class="profile-title">Senior Data Engineer & Creator</p>
				
				<div class="profile-bio">
					<p>
						I am a Senior Data Engineer at Amazon with over 15 years of experience building resilient, scalable data platforms. My current focus is defining the "Control Plane" of data—designing strategies, governance frameworks, and self-service platforms that serve 700+ internal customers.
					</p>
					<p>
						Beyond scaling pipelines, I am fascinated by GenAI/ML infrastructure (like building RAG services and Feature Stores), engineering culture, and mentoring as an Amazon Bar Raiser. Thinking Buffer is my outlet for abstracting daily office challenges into generalized lessons and exploring engineering culture, architectures, and leadership.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="profile-links">
					<a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/neerav-kumar-aa232b9a/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="profile-link-btn">
						<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="currentColor">
							<path d="M20.447 20.452h-3.554v-5.569c0-1.328-.027-3.037-1.852-3.037-1.853 0-2.136 1.445-2.136 2.939v5.667H9.351V9h3.414v1.561h.046c.477-.9 1.637-1.85 3.37-1.85 3.601 0 4.267 2.37 4.267 5.455v6.286zM5.337 7.433c-1.144 0-2.063-.926-2.063-2.065 0-1.138.92-2.063 2.063-2.063 1.14 0 2.064.925 2.064 2.063 0 1.139-.925 2.065-2.064 2.065zm1.782 13.019H3.555V9h3.564v11.452zM22.225 0H1.771C.792 0 0 .774 0 1.729v20.542C0 23.227.792 24 1.771 24h20.451C23.2 24 24 23.227 24 22.271V1.729C24 .774 23.2 0 22.222 0h.003z"/>
						</svg>
						LinkedIn
					</a>
					<a href="https://github.com/kr-neerav" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="profile-link-btn">
						<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="currentColor">
							<path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M12 2C6.477 2 2 6.477 2 12c0 4.42 2.865 8.166 6.839 9.489.5.092.682-.217.682-.482 0-.237-.008-.866-.013-1.7-2.782.603-3.369-1.34-3.369-1.34-.454-1.156-1.11-1.464-1.11-1.464-.908-.62.069-.608.069-.608 1.003.07 1.531 1.03 1.531 1.03.892 1.529 2.341 1.087 2.91.831.092-.646.35-1.086.636-1.336-2.22-.253-4.555-1.11-4.555-4.943 0-1.091.39-1.984 1.029-2.683-.103-.253-.446-1.27.098-2.647 0 0 .84-.269 2.75 1.025A9.564 9.564 0 0112 6.844c.85.004 1.705.115 2.504.337 1.909-1.294 2.747-1.025 2.747-1.025.546 1.377.203 2.394.1 2.646.64.699 1.026 1.592 1.026 2.683 0 3.842-2.337 4.687-4.565 4.935.359.309.678.919.678 1.852 0 1.336-.012 2.415-.012 2.743 0 .267.18.579.688.481C19.137 20.162 22 16.418 22 12c0-5.523-4.477-10-10-10z"/>
						</svg>
						GitHub
					</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</div>

	<!-- Pillars Section -->
	<section class="pillars-section">
		<h2 class="section-title">Focus Areas</h2>
		<div class="pillars-grid">
			<div class="card pillar-card">
				<div class="pillar-icon">
					<svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
						<path d="M4 19.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 17H20"></path>
						<path d="M6.5 2H20v20H6.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 4 19.5v-15A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 2z"></path>
					</svg>
				</div>
				<h3 class="pillar-title">Deep Articles</h3>
				<p class="pillar-description">
					Writing that explores technical problems, automation, systems design, and leadership. The objective is to strip away the company-specific context of office incidents and deliver general, actionable frameworks you can apply directly to your own team or codebase.
				</p>
				<div class="card-tags">
					<span class="tag">Abstracting the Office</span>
					<span class="tag">Systems & Leadership</span>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="card pillar-card">
				<div class="pillar-icon">
					<svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
						<polygon points="12 2 2 7 12 12 22 7 12 2"></polygon>
						<polyline points="2 17 12 22 22 17"></polyline>
						<polyline points="2 12 12 17 22 12"></polyline>
					</svg>
				</div>
				<h3 class="pillar-title">Architecture & Platform Design</h3>
				<p class="pillar-description">
					Deep dives into building scalable data systems, self-service developer control planes, and robust distributed infrastructures that stand up to massive production scale.
				</p>
				<div class="card-tags">
					<span class="tag">Platform Engineering</span>
					<span class="tag">Data Systems</span>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>

<style>
	/* Hero Section */
	.about-hero {
		margin-bottom: 4rem;
		padding-top: 2rem;
		text-align: center;
	}
	
	.about-hero h1 {
		font-size: 3.5rem;
		line-height: 1.1;
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
		color: #1A1A1A;
		letter-spacing: -0.03em;
	}
	
	.about-hero .subtitle {
		font-size: 1.25rem;
		color: #4A4A4A;
		max-width: 650px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		line-height: 1.5;
	}

	/* Two-column Layout */
	.about-split {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 0.8fr;
		gap: 4rem;
		margin-bottom: 5rem;
		align-items: start;
	}

	.section-title {
		font-size: 1.8rem;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
		color: #1A1A1A;
	}

	/* Narrative Content Styling */
	.narrative h3 {
		font-size: 1.25rem;
		margin-top: 2rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
		color: #1A1A1A;
	}

	.narrative h3:first-of-type {
		margin-top: 0;
	}

	.narrative p {
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		color: #444;
		line-height: 1.6;
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
	}

	.narrative strong {
		color: #000;
		font-weight: 600;
	}

	/* Profile Card Styling */
	.profile-card {
		padding: 2.5rem 2rem;
		align-items: center;
		text-align: center;
		background: var(--card-bg);
	}

	.profile-avatar-large {
		width: 120px;
		height: 120px;
		border-radius: 50%;
		overflow: hidden;
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
		box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
		background-color: #F8F9FA;
		border: 4px solid #FFF;
	}

	.profile-avatar-large img {
		width: 100%;
		height: 100%;
		object-fit: cover;
	}

	.profile-name {
		font-size: 1.4rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
		color: #1A1A1A;
	}

	.profile-title {
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		color: #666;
		font-weight: 500;
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
	}

	.profile-bio {
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		color: #555;
		line-height: 1.6;
		text-align: left;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}

	.profile-bio p {
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}

	.profile-bio p:last-child {
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}

	.profile-links {
		display: flex;
		gap: 1rem;
		width: 100%;
	}

	.profile-link-btn {
		flex: 1;
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
		background-color: #F1F5F9;
		border-radius: 10px;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		color: #334155;
		transition: all 0.2s ease;
	}

	.profile-link-btn:hover {
		background-color: #E2E8F0;
		color: #0F172A;
		opacity: 1;
		transform: translateY(-1px);
	}

	/* Pillars Section */
	.pillars-section {
		margin-bottom: 3rem;
	}

	.pillars-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
		gap: 2rem;
	}

	.pillar-card {
		padding: 2.5rem;
		background: var(--card-bg);
		height: 100%;
	}

	.pillar-icon {
		width: 48px;
		height: 48px;
		border-radius: 12px;
		background-color: #E5EEF9;
		color: #3B82F6;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
	}

	.pillar-card:nth-child(2) .pillar-icon {
		background-color: #FFEEDB;
		color: #F97316;
	}

	.pillar-title {
		font-size: 1.25rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
		color: #1A1A1A;
	}

	.pillar-description {
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		color: #555;
		line-height: 1.6;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
		flex-grow: 1;
	}

	/* Responsive Queries */
	@media (max-width: 900px) {
		.about-split {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 3rem;
		}

		.pillars-grid {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 1.5rem;
		}

		.about-hero h1 {
			font-size: 2.75rem;
		}
	}
</style>
